// glyphs — the two baked faces, as data.
//
// Rasterised from Segoe UI and stored here so that a program which wants
// a line of readable text on a framebuffer does not have to carry six
// hundred lines of table of its own. Two programs written against smalt
// each did, and their tables had drifted into two slightly different
// fonts before anyone noticed.
//
// A glyph row is two `i32` words of fourteen pixels, **2 bits per pixel**
// — four coverage levels, so the text is anti-aliased against whatever it
// lands on rather than punched out in one colour. At 14 px that is the
// difference between a UI you read and one you decipher.
//
// Fourteen pixels to a word and not sixteen, so the top bit is never set:
// an array literal takes its element type from its values, and one word
// past `i32`'s range would retype the whole table.
//
// Two faces, because the two jobs differ. `ui*` (Segoe UI 14) draws every
// label, column and row; `big*` (Segoe UI Bold 22) draws headline figures
// over the subset of characters those figures use — a full ASCII range at
// that size would be several thousand rows of table for glyphs nothing
// prints, which is why `bigIndex` is a map and `UI_FIRST` an offset.
//
// Both are functions returning a table rather than top-level constants: a
// top-level initialiser must be a literal (E0720). `BitmapFont` calls each
// once and holds the buffer for the life of the program, which is why the
// per-call allocation is not a per-frame one.
//
// Everything here is `pub(crate)`: `render::text` is the only reader, and
// a program that wants its own face hands `BitmapFont::fromTables` its own
// arrays rather than reaching in here.

/** Stored pixel rows per glyph in the UI face. */
pub(crate) const UI_H : i32 = 14;
/** Row 0 of a UI glyph, as an offset from the text baseline. */
pub(crate) const UI_TOP : i32 = -11;
/** Stored pixel rows per glyph in the headline face. */
pub(crate) const BIG_H : i32 = 22;
/** Row 0 of a headline glyph, as an offset from the text baseline. */
pub(crate) const BIG_TOP : i32 = -17;
/** First ASCII code the UI face covers; below it renders as a space. */
pub(crate) const UI_FIRST : i32 = 32;
/** Last ASCII code the UI face covers. */
pub(crate) const UI_LAST : i32 = 126;

/**
 * Pen advance of each UI glyph, indexed by `code - UI_FIRST`.
 */
pub(crate) fn uiWidths() : i32[] {
    return [
        4, 4, 5, 8, 8, 11, 11, 3, 4, 4, 6, 10, 3, 6, 3, 5, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8,
        8, 8, 3, 3, 10, 10, 10, 6, 13, 9, 8, 9, 10, 7, 7, 10, 10, 4, 5, 8, 7, 13, 10, 11,
        8, 11, 8, 7, 7, 10, 9, 13, 8, 8, 8, 4, 5, 4, 10, 6, 4, 7, 8, 6, 8, 7, 4, 8,
        8, 3, 3, 7, 3, 12, 8, 8, 8, 8, 5, 6, 5, 8, 7, 10, 6, 7, 6, 4, 3, 4, 10
    ];
}

